<title>USA: U.S. mortgage application volume dips in latest wk.</title>
<headline>U.S. mortgage application volume dips in latest wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The volume of U.S. mortgage applications fell 0.7 percent in the week ended October 4, according to a Mortgage Bankers Association of America weekly survey.</p>
<p>Specifically, the volume of applications to refinance mortgages rose 0.3 percent in the latest survey week, while applications to purchase mortgages slipped 0.9 percent.</p>
<p>The seasonally adjusted refinancing index rose 0.3 percent to 272.3 from 271.4 the previous week, it said.</p>
<p>The purchase index fell 1.0 percent to 182.4 in the latest survey from 184.3 in the previous week, it said.  </p>
